s have historically played&#10;a pivotal role in creating vibrant pigments utilized across&#10;artistic mediums such as ceramics, paintings, and glass&#10;mosaics. Despite their extensive historical use, our&#10;understanding of the mechanisms governing transition met...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 2&#10;domain: same_field&#10;radius: R1&#10;title: Exploring the Role and Variability of 3d Transition&#10;Metal Complexes in Artistic Coloration through a Bottom-Up&#10;Scientific Approach&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Bottom-up multiscale structure–property&#10;mapping from molecular/coordination origins to macroscopic&#10;color behavior', 'Integration of spectroscopy and&#10;computational chemistry to infer electronic transitions and&#10;local coordination effects', 'Explicit modeling of processing-&#10;condition variability as a driver of final pigment color and&#10;performance', 'Analytical-data fusion with technique-specific&#10;uncertainty and scope awareness']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the candidate’s bottom-up multiscale&#10;framework into a predictive pigment architecture that links&#10;local coordination, oxidation state, lattice distortion, and&#10;electronic transitions to optical scattering, stability,&#10;toxicity, and NIR reflectance. Use spectroscopy-informed...&#10;justification: The candidate provides a transferable&#10;organizing principle: connect microscopic coordination&#10;chemistry and electronic structure to macroscopic color&#10;through multiscale, data-integrated modeling. This directly&#10;addresses the original problem’s missing predictive mechanism&#10;linkin...&#10;abstract: Transition metal complexes have historically played&#10;a pivotal role in creating vibrant pigments utilized across&#10;artistic mediums such as ceramics, paintings, and glass&#10;mosaics. Despite their extensive historical use, our&#10;understanding of the mechanisms governing transition met...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 3&#10;domain: computer_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Harnessing surrogate models for data-efficient&#10;predictive chemistry: descriptors &lt;i&gt;vs.&lt;/i&gt; learned hidden&#10;representations&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Surrogate models trained on scarce&#10;chemistry data', 'Learned hidden representations as&#10;transferable features', 'Using latent model features instead&#10;of only explicit predicted descriptors', 'Data-efficient&#10;downstream property prediction']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the surrogate-model strategy by&#10;training intermediate predictive models on available pigment&#10;data, such as coordination geometry, oxidation state, lattice&#10;distortion, electronic transition energies, or DFT-derived&#10;properties, then extract their hidden representations as...&#10;justification: The candidate paper provides a transferable&#10;principle for scarce scientific data: hidden representations&#10;learned by surrogate models can encode useful mechanistic&#10;structure-property relationships better than explicit&#10;predicted descriptors. This maps directly onto the pigment&#10;p...&#10;abstract: When data are scarce, surrogate models trained on QM&#10;descriptors help. We report that their hidden features, not&#10;the predicted descriptors, provide superior inputs for&#10;downstream predictive chemistry tasks.&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 4&#10;domain: computer_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Combining Machine Learning and Computational Chemistry&#10;for Predictive Insights Into Chemical Systems&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Hybrid machine-learning + computational-&#10;chemistry predictive modeling', 'Physics-informed descriptors&#10;encoding local coordination, oxidation state, and lattice&#10;environment', 'Surrogate models for expensive&#10;quantum/mechanical property calculations', 'Multi-task or&#10;multi-objective prediction linking structure to optical,&#10;stability, toxicity, and reflectance properties', 'Active&#10;learning / high-throughput screening to guide empirical&#10;pigment discovery']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the candidate’s ML-plus-computational-&#10;chemistry framework into pigment science by constructing&#10;physics-informed descriptors for host-dopant coordination,&#10;oxidation state, lattice distortion, and electronic structure,&#10;then training surrogate models to predict color intens...&#10;justification: The candidate paper provides a transferable&#10;abstraction: combining mechanistic chemical modeling with&#10;machine learning to create predictive structure-property&#10;frameworks. This maps directly onto the pigment problem’s need&#10;to move from empirical discovery toward generalizable p...&#10;abstract: Machine learning models are poised to make a&#10;transformative impact on chemical sciences by dramatically&#10;accelerating computational algorithms and amplifying insights&#10;available from computational chemistry methods. However,&#10;achieving this requires a confluence and coaction of e...&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 5&#10;domain: physics&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Computational Studies of the Photophysical, Structural,&#10;and Catalytic Properties of Complex Chemical Systems&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Computational structure-property&#10;prediction workflows for complex chemical systems',&#10;'Integration of theoretical calculations, experimental&#10;observations, and databases into predictive models',&#10;'Prediction of photophysical properties from local electronic&#10;and structural descriptors', 'Statistical or machine-learning&#10;modeling of chemical reactivity, stability, and functional&#10;properties']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the candidate’s computational&#10;chemistry framework into a pigment-discovery pipeline that&#10;computes local coordination, dopant oxidation state, lattice&#10;distortion, and electronic-transition descriptors, then links&#10;them through statistical or machine-learning models to powd...&#10;justification: The candidate paper embodies a transferable&#10;abstraction: using computational modeling and data-driven&#10;integration to predict complex structure-property&#10;relationships. This maps directly onto the pigment problem’s&#10;missing predictive mechanism connecting atomic-scale&#10;coordinatio...&#10;abstract: Computational chemistry employs mathematical&#10;algorithms, statistics, and large databases to integrate&#10;chemical theory with experimental observations. Computational&#10;modeling allows us to make predictions concerning molecular&#10;properties and reactivity that ultimately lead to acc..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#f9cb9c;strokeColor=#b45f06;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="10774" width="620" height="2940" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step7_analogy_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step7" target="step7_analogy_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step8" value="Step 8 Inspiration Selection&#10;status: completed&#10;selected_count: 2&#10;round: 3" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="60" y="13814" width="232" height="96" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step_step7_step_step8" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step7" target="step_step8"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step8_selected_panel" value="Step 8 Selected Inspiration&#10;count: 2&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 3&#10;domain: computer_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Harnessing surrogate models for data-efficient&#10;predictive chemistry: descriptors &lt;i&gt;vs.&lt;/i&gt; learned hidden&#10;representations&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Surrogate models trained on scarce&#10;chemistry data', 'Learned hidden representations as&#10;transferable features', 'Using latent model features instead&#10;of only explicit predicted descriptors', 'Data-efficient&#10;downstream property prediction']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the surrogate-model strategy by&#10;training intermediate predictive models on available pigment&#10;data, such as coordination geometry, oxidation state, lattice&#10;distortion, electronic transition energies, or DFT-derived&#10;properties, then extract their hidden representations as...&#10;justification: The candidate paper provides a transferable&#10;principle for scarce scientific data: hidden representations&#10;learned by surrogate models can encode useful mechanistic&#10;structure-property relationships better than explicit&#10;predicted descriptors. This maps directly onto the pigment&#10;p...&#10;abstract: When data are scarce, surrogate models trained on QM&#10;descriptors help. We report that their hidden features, not&#10;the predicted descriptors, provide superior inputs for&#10;downstream predictive chemistry tasks.&#10;&#10;candidate_id: 4&#10;domain: computer_science&#10;radius: R2&#10;title: Combining Machine Learning and Computational Chemistry&#10;for Predictive Insights Into Chemical Systems&#10;plausible: True&#10;combination_points: ['Hybrid machine-learning + computational-&#10;chemistry predictive modeling', 'Physics-informed descriptors&#10;encoding local coordination, oxidation state, and lattice&#10;environment', 'Surrogate models for expensive&#10;quantum/mechanical property calculations', 'Multi-task or&#10;multi-objective prediction linking structure to optical,&#10;stability, toxicity, and reflectance properties', 'Active&#10;learning / high-throughput screening to guide empirical&#10;pigment discovery']&#10;combination_plan: Adapt the candidate’s ML-plus-computational-&#10;chemistry framework into pigment science by constructing&#10;physics-informed descriptors for host-dopant coordination,&#10;oxidation state, lattice distortion, and electronic structure,&#10;then training surrogate models to predict color intens...&#10;justification: The candidate paper provides a transferable&#10;abstraction: combining mechanistic chemical modeling with&#10;machine learning to create predictive structure-property&#10;frameworks. This maps directly onto the pigment problem’s need&#10;to move from empirical discovery toward generalizable p...&#10;abstract: Machine learning models are poised to make a&#10;transformative impact on chemical sciences by dramatically&#10;accelerating computational algorithms and amplifying insights&#10;available from computational chemistry methods. However,&#10;achieving this requires a confluence and coaction of e..." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#ead1dc;strokeColor=#a64d79;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="13814" width="620" height="1212" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step8_selected_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step8_selected_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step_step9" value="Step 9 Idea Generation&#10;status: completed&#10;idea_count: 1&#10;round: 3" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#d5e8d4;strokeColor=#82b366;fontSize=12;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="60" y="15126" width="220" height="96" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step_step8_step_step9" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step8" target="step_step9"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="step9_ideas_panel" value="Step 9 Idea Generation + Novelty Check&#10;count: 1&#10;&#10;1. Latent Defect-Optical Surrogates for Discovering High-NIR Red&#10;Mn/Cr Oxide Pigments&#10;novelty_level: medium&#10;motivation: The original query asks whether more color pigments&#10;can be discovered. The answer is yes if new pigment materials,&#10;not new perceptual color categories, are found by design. Red&#10;Mn-oxide and Cr-doped oxide systems already show that visible&#10;red color can be coupled to near-infrared reflectance [Gramm et&#10;al., 2020](https://doi.org/10.1002/zaac.202000274) [Divya et&#10;al., 2021](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ceramint.2021.07...&#10;methods: 1. Fixed-hue defect library with morphology and phase&#10;controls: Use Li2MnO3 as the primary red host because it is a&#10;rare Mn4+ red oxide and a NIR-reflective pigment target [Gramm&#10;et al., 2020](https://doi.org/10.1002/zaac.202000274). Prepare&#10;one phase-pure batch, then split it into aliquots and anneal at&#10;the same temperature and time under different oxygen partial&#10;pressures. This varies only the oxygen-vacancy and Mn3+/Mn4+&#10;defect population. Thermal treatment is known to alter local&#10;transition-metal environment...&#10;novelty_justification: The closest existing combination is the&#10;Li2MnO3 high-NIR red pigment work plus Cr3+-doped LaAlO3 red/NIR&#10;pigment work, reinforced by YInMn structure-&#10;optical/thermochromic studies and morphology/scattering&#10;references. Those references already establish the target&#10;materials, the red/NIR property goal, and the relevance of local&#10;coordination, defects/valence, and particle morphology. The&#10;proposal adds a fixed-host, f...&#10;improvement_suggestions: [&quot;Sharpen the mechanistic claim from 'a&#10;latent representation helps prediction' to 'a low-dimensional,&#10;causally identifiable defect-loss coordinate is the minimal&#10;sufficient mediator of NIR loss at fixed hue.' Define that&#10;coordinate, for example as integrated oscillator strength of&#10;Mn3+/Mn4+ intervalence plus oxygen-vacancy polaron absorption,&#10;and validate it through interventions such as pO2 annealing,&#10;aliovalent substitution, or vacancy trapping, while testing&#10;invariance across hosts.&quot;, 'Introduce a hue-NIR decoupling&#10;principle or metric, such as fixed-hue NIR efficiency defined as&#10;scattering-corrected NIR reflectance per unit visible hue&#10;strength, and show the latent defect-optical model can optimize&#10;this metric by suppressing only the NIR-loss channel while&#10;preserving the hue-producing transition. This turns the workflow&#10;into a distinct design rule rather than a general surrogate&#10;pipeline.', 'Make transferability a conceptual test: require the&#10;learned defect-optical manifold to predict out-of-sample hosts&#10;only when channel labels and physical constraints are preserved,&#10;and demonstrate that a universal defect-loss manifold transfers&#10;between Mn and Cr hosts despite different compositions. This&#10;would elevate the contribution from component assembly to a&#10;generalizable mechanistic representation.']" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontSize=11;align=left;verticalAlign=top;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry as="geometry" x="360" y="15126" width="680" height="1104" /></mxCell><mxCell id="edge_step9_ideas_panel" value="" style="edgeStyle=none;rounded=0;orthogonalLoop=0;jettySize=0;html=0;endArrow=block;" edge="1" parent="1" source="step_step9" target="step9_ideas_panel"><mxGeometry as="geometry" relative="1" /></mxCell><mxCell id="retrieval_1" value="Retrieval 1&#10;step: step1&#10;command: search-papers&#10;cache_hit: False&#10;paper_count: 18&#10;&#10;Parameters&#10;query_text: combinatorial exploration of ternary and&#10;quaternary oxide pigment phase spaces&#10;keywords: [{'text': 'combinatorial exploration', 'score':&#10;10}, {'text': 'exploration ternary', 'score': 9}, {'text':&#10;'ternary quaternary', 'score': 8}, {'text': 'quaternary&#10;oxide', 'score': 7}, {'text': 'oxide pigment', 'score':&#10;6}]&#10;source_type: idea_text&#10;top_k: 18&#10;retrieval_mode: hybrid&#10;target_field: Chemistry&#10;&#10;Returned Papers&#10;1. Production of iron oxide pigments using metallurgical&#10;wastes (2024) [score=0.6741]&#10;Abstract: To produce paints and varnish coatings, there is&#10;an opportunity to use a waste of metallurgical production&#10;of Yakovlevsky mining and processing complex, Cherepovets,&#10;Russia. This waste contains iron oxide as iron oxide&#10;pigment. It could be used as an analogue to iron oxide&#10;pig...&#10;&#10;2. Integrated methodologies for qualitative and&#10;quantitative characterization of historical pigments&#10;(2014) [score=0.6571]&#10;Abstract: ti iv ve e c ch ha ar ra ac ct te er ri iz za at&#10;ti io on n o of f h hi is st to or ri ic ca al l p pi ig&#10;gm me en nt ts s Contents 6.4 RAMAN quantitive method 6.5&#10;Spectrophotometric quantitive method Bibliography&#10;Discussion and Conclusions Acknowledgments Chapter 1&#10;-Diagnosti...&#10;&#10;3. Properties of Metal Oxide Pigments Surface Modified&#10;with Polyaniline Phosphate and Polypyrrole Phosphate in&#10;Corrosion Protective Organic Coatings (2016)&#10;[score=0.6536]&#10;Abstract: The objective of this work was to describe the&#10;properties of metal oxide-based pigments whose surface has&#10;been coated with a conductive polymer, if used as pigments&#10;in organic coating materials. The perovskite-type pigments&#10;were synthesized by high-temperature solid-phase reac...&#10;&#10;4. EFFECT OF Ni DOPING AND SYNTHESIS TEMPERATURE ON THE&#10;PROPERTIES OF NIR-REFLECTIVE ZnFe₂O₄ BLACK PIGMENTS (2020)&#10;[score=0.6176]&#10;Abstract: NIR-reflective Ni-doped ZnFe 2 O 4 black&#10;pigments with the general formula of Zn (1-x) Ni x Fe 2 O&#10;4 have been synthesized by a conventional solid-state&#10;reaction of ZnO, Fe 2 O 3 and NiO. The effect of Ni doping&#10;was studied by adding various amounts of NiO, with x&#10;ranging from...&#10;&#10;5. Towards the Discrimination between Natural and&#10;Synthetic Pigments: The Case of Ultramarine (2023)&#10;[score=0.6162]&#10;Abstract: Ultramarine has been for centuries one of the&#10;most highly prized pigments of all traditional artists’&#10;materials, due to its durability, excellent color, and its&#10;intrinsic value. For the production of the blue pigment&#10;Ultramarine, the rare semiprecious stone Lapis Lazuli has&#10;be...&#10;&#10;6. Exploration of New Phosphors Using a Mineral-Inspired&#10;Approach in Combination with Solution Parallel Synthesis&#10;(2013) [score=0.611]&#10;Abstract: The concept, as well as the methodology of using&#10;a mineral-inspired approach in combination with solution&#10;parallel synthesis (SPS) for exploration of new phosphors&#10;among Na/Sr(Ba)/Al-silicate and Zr(Ti)-silicate minerals,&#10;is reported. By employing the proposed approach, we hav...&#10;&#10;7. Crystal structure prediction of organic pigments:&#10;quinacridone as an example (2007) [score=0.5733]&#10;Abstract: The structures of the alpha, beta and gamma&#10;polymorphs of quinacridone (Pigment Violet 19) were&#10;predicted using Polymorph Predictor software in&#10;combination with X-ray powder diffraction patterns of&#10;limited quality. After generation and energy minimization&#10;of the possible struc...&#10;&#10;8. Synthesis and characterization of inorganic colour&#10;pigment from spent acid (2018) [score=0.5657]&#10;Abstract: This paper proposes a new method of recycling&#10;spent acid from local cold rolling industry into iron&#10;oxide pigment that to be applied to the roof tiles.&#10;Pickling is a process in which a hot-rolled steel that has&#10;rusty scale is dipped into hydrochloric acid prior to&#10;further proc...&#10;&#10;9. Commentary: The Materials Project: A materials genome&#10;approach to accelerating materials innovation (2013)&#10;[score=0.5533]&#10;Abstract: Accelerating the discovery of advanced materials&#10;is essential for human welfare and sustainable, clean&#10;energy. In this paper, we introduc